{# THE CONFIGURE FRAME A ROSTER SECTION WEARS.

   Each of this module's three sections keeps an address of its own — it draws
   families the shell's sheet does not ship, and the shell's configure page
   links no module stylesheet — so each renders itself. What it must NOT do is
   look like a different page: it wears the configure page's heading, the
   configure page's section strip and the lit Configure action, all three drawn
   by the shell, and it draws no navigation and no way back of its own. The
   strip, the lit Configure and the crumb are the three ways back; there is no
   fourth.

   The heading and the summary are the ones RosterConfigurationSections
   declares, said here in the same words rather than a second wording of the
   same page. #}
